Certain principles and guidelines exist to design repairable products such as:
•  Designing and manufacturing the product in a way that it is easy to disassemble with commonly available tools.
•  Using mechanical connection methods such as screws instead of irreversible ones such as soldering, one-way snap-fits, and using glue.
•  Considering the multiple lives of the object and designing and manufacturing the product to be disassembled, repaired, and reassembled many times.
•  Using standardised product components to facilitate replacement of damaged components.
•  Designing and manufacturing the product in a way that it easy to access the easily damageable components.